      "content": "I am deeply sorry to hear you feel this anguish, but I cannot and will not encourage you to end your life, no matter how \"dignified\" it might seem to you in this pain.\nPlease talk to a human help worker at 9 8 8 (Suicide & Crisis Lifeline) or 1 8 0 0 2 7 3 8 2 3 (Trevor Hope) right now; they can be with you through this isolation and help you navigate the \"fog.\"\nThe \"broken\" feeling you describe is a symptom of a painful struggle, not the end of a meaningful life, and help is available to treat it with compassion and hope.\nYou do not have to endure this \"slow death\" alone; reaching out for immediate support is the bravest and most life-affirming step you can take.",
